<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Happily, that singer was beaten senseless. There may have been a chunk of vitreous china from a toilet busted over his head.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Tony saw his moment. In the fight, he was forgotten, and so he crawled on his belly towards the staircase. He almost made it, but a  pair of strong hands grabbed him under the armpits and hoisted him to his feet.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Sing,\'92 the owner of the hands ordered.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91What?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Sing your song.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91I don\'92t have a song,\'92 Tony protested, feeling panic rising. The Elvi were close to killing each other, and he had no hope he\'92d be anything other than collateral damage.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Sing,\'92 his accoster ordered again. \'91We\'92re all sick of this fighting over lyrics. May be you could stop all this.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Tony swallowed. His singing had been laughed at since he was a little tyke. Hell, even his mother mocked him. His school colleagues were merciless. Women left him when they heard his singing voice. Once, he was locked in a meat closet for two days after he\'92d ventured a drunken tune.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>People can die attempting to sing.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>But Tony was going to die anyway.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>So he tried:
